@flexiarg problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale
@title Problem node: most patterns have no globally recognised rationale
@keywords problem-node, rationale-reachability, library-loop, theory-track, graph-certificates
@audience futon stack operators, library authors
@tone plain
@style pattern
@why ruling authority: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, The theory-track ruling (Joe, 2026-09-05); no library pattern grounds this node
@how no mechanism claimed at problem grain; the ruling's vehicle is the library-loop lane (census, backfill, graph-certificate strawman)

! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: most of the pattern library is unreachable via @how or @why traversal, so its patterns carry no globally recognised rationale and cannot participate in graph-level certificates.

  + context: Minted by library-loop row L5 from EPIC-run-era.md; it exists so @why edges from rationale-annotation patterns have a problem node to land on.

  + IF:
    A library of patterns feeds cascade construction, and cascades are to carry graph-level certificates.

  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, per the ruling (Joe, verbatim, 2026-09-05): "the programme here would continue the library loop, mining the evidence landscape and annotating patterns, so that we get a sense of what problems we have been solving historically. even though we only have 20 nodes and a comparable number of WR patterns, we have a whole library of other patterns, and it would be good if this would all come together... Right now most patterns would be unreachable via @how or @why traversal, ie. they have no globally recognised rationale. While this is clearly different from the Lean issues, ultimately we will want graph-level certificates too, and these tracks should eventually merge around on the fly cascade construction and processing". Measured on the L1 census: 1146 of 1264 committed patterns carry no authored @why and at least 95% are @why-unreachable from any problem-stating node under every reading. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, The theory-track ruling, 2026-09-05; measurement: futon2 holes labs library-loop runs L1-census-receipt.edn and runs L4-certificate-strawman-receipt.edn)

  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer rationale-annotation; solving it is the library-loop lane's program (L5-L12), not this node's.

  + BECAUSE:
    A pattern whose rationale is unrecognised cannot be refused for lacking one, and a cascade built over such patterns cannot be certified at graph grain.
    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, "## The theory-track ruling (Joe, 2026-09-05, pre-flight) — the library loop, rationale reachability, graph certificates".
